Description: Fairphone (Gen. 6) support for Mobian
 Device glue for the Fairphone (Gen. 6) (Qualcomm SM7635 "Milos") on Mobian:
  - a boot write guard in place of qcom-phone-utils' zz-qcom-bootimg
    (diverted): it writes the boot partition only when it already holds
    Mobian, its AVB data is intact and the new image fits; fp6-boot-avb moves
    the stock vbmeta to the end of the partition so larger images fit;
  - an initramfs post-update hook, so package-triggered initramfs rebuilds
    reach the boot partition too;
  - fp6-make-bootimg, to build a boot image without writing it;
  - the FP6 firmware and touchscreen modules in the initramfs (without
    modem.mbn, which doesn't fit; the modem is started from the root
    filesystem);
  - droid-juicer: load erofs first, and reboot to fastboot while the phone is
    RAM-booted;
  - AudioReach topology (built from source), UCM, and echo cancellation for
    calls, with imsd's call audio routed through it;
  - sensor udev rules and module loading;
  - fp6-lte-pin, which keeps the modem on LTE (a carrier workaround, see
    /etc/default/fp6-lte-pin);
  - no system suspend, and an apt pin that keeps kernels that can't boot the
    phone off it.
